 \nL193: ### pH\nL194: \nL195: 3.0-4.5\nL196: ### useful pH range\nL197: \nL198: 6.1-7.5\nL199: \nL200: ### pKa (25 °C)\nL201: \nL202: 6.8\nL203: \nL204: ### mp\nL205: \nL206: >220 °C (dec.) (lit.)\nL207: \nL208: ### solubility\nL209: \nL210: water: 0.523 g/mL, clear, colorless\nL211: \nL212: ### application(s)\nL213: \nL214: diagnostic assay manufacturing\nL215: \nL216: ### storage temp.\nL217: \nL218: room temp\nL219: \nL220: ### SMILES string\nL221: \nL222: NC(=O)CNCCS(O)(=O)=O\nL223: \nL224: ### InChI\nL225: \nL226: 1S/C4H10N2O4S/c5-4(7)3-6-1-2-11(8,9)10/h6H,1-3H2,(H2,5,7)(H,8,9,10)\nL227: \nL228: ### InChI key\nL229: \nL230: DBXNUXBLKRLWFA-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL231: \nL232: Description\nL233: ### General description\nL234: \nL235: N-(2-Acetamido)-2-aminoethanesulfonic acid (ACES) is a zwitterionic buffer used in biochemistry and molecular biology research. It is one of the Good′s buffers with a pH range of 6.15 - 8.35. The preferred range of ACES buffer in an aqueous solution is 6.1 - 7.5.\nL236: ### Application\nL237: \nL238: ACES has been used:\nL239:   * as a component of buffered charcoal yeast extract (BYCE) agar for plating bacteria culture and Buffered Yeast Extract (BYE) liquid medium to culture bacteria\nL240:   * to study the impact of the pH shift on the thermal inactivation of bacterial (Bacillus subtills) spores\nL241:   * as a buffer system to study the depolymerization of starch by α-amylase during exposure to hydrostatic pressure.\nL242: It is also suitable for use: as buffers for both agarose and polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis; in the isoelectric focusing of proteins; in the analysis of bacterial autolysins in a discontinuous sodium dodecyl sulphate-polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis (SDS-PAGE) system.\nL243: ### Other Notes\nL244: \nL245: The product is intended for laboratory use only, and it is not suitable for drug, household, or other purposes.\nL246: \nL247: * * *\nL248: \nL249: ## Compare Similar Items\nL250: \nL251: 【18†View Full Compariso